{{Quote|They were last seen in turbolift G-27.''"<br />"''I thought all turbolifts were locked down.''"<br />"''They were, sir, but it appears they were tampered with.|A stormtrooper and Pyre|<ref name="The Escape" />}}
'''Turbolift G-27''' was a [[turbolift]] aboard the [[First Order]] [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]]<ref name="The Escape" /> ''[[Thunderer]]''.<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date" /> after the [[Desertion|defecting]] [[First Order TIE fighter pilot|TIE pilot]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] and the [[Resistance]] operatives [[Kazuda Xiono]] and [[Jarek Yeager]] escaped from the [[Star Destroyer|ship's]] [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]], they made their way to the turbolift and discovered it was offline. Xiono then requested the [[BB-series astromech droid]] [[CB-23]] activate it for them, which the [[droid]] did, allowing the trio to escape from [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]]. Afterward, a [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper (Thunderer's bridge)|stormtrooper]] informed [[Commander]] [[Pyre]] and [[Agent]] [[Tierny]] of the last known location of the three at tubrolift G-27. Not long thereafter, the Star Destroyer, along with turbolift G-27, was destroyed in the [[Barabesh system]] by the [[Team Colossus|residents]] of the [[Supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]] ''[[Colossus]]''.<ref name="The Escape" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Turbolift G-27 appeared in part two of the two-part episode "[[The Escape (episode)|The Escape]],"<ref name="The Escape" /> the finale of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season Two|second season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', which aired on [[January 26]], [[2020]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref>

